# M10.3 acceptance: Single Page navigation on tests/data/slides-16x9.pdf (8 slides;
# slide N has "Slide N" in large type and "Point <word>: distinct body text for slide N.",
# see tests/data/make_slides_pdf.py). Run through tests/acceptance/m10.3.sh, which
# copies the deck into a saved project and turns on the developer login, so the chat
# input is shown. The plain command
#   scripts/shot.sh -o <repo>/.verify/m10.3/<impl|review|tester> -s tests/acceptance/m10.3.steps -- ./build/app/agentic-reader tests/data/slides-16x9.pdf
# runs the same steps, but shows the API key banner instead of the chat input.
#
# Interface choices where the spec is silent (the implementer conforms or files a TEST DISPUTE):
#   - The toolbar gains "Previous" and "Next" buttons after the "Single Page" toggle, in
#     that order. Their centers are about (540, 48) and (610, 48).
#   - Button 5 is one wheel notch down (next slide). Button 4 is one notch up (previous).
#   - Each step ends with a 0.3 s pause. Two notches inside 150 ms therefore need one
#     step: run xdotool click --repeat 2 --delay 40 5.
#
# Geometry at the default 1400x900 window, as in m10.2.steps: toolbar y 28..68, zoom
# combo (35,48), page entry (320,48), "/ 8" at about (360,48), "Single Page" toggle
# x 384..489. PDF pane x 225..980, y 69..875, center (602,472). Chat input at about
# (1180, 800). Single Page at 76%: the slide is at x 237..968, y 267..677, grey above and
# below it. (602,150) is grey in Single Page and a blank part of slide 3 in Continuous, so
# a click there only moves focus to the PDF view.
#
# Every shot says the page entry ("N / 8") and the slide on screen. Combo "76%" throughout.
wait 3
click 602 150

# Single Page at open (the deck is 16:9, so it opens in Single Page). "Slide 1" and
# "Point alpha" are centered in the grey frame. Entry "1 / 8".
shot slide-1

# Right goes forward. "Slide 2" and "Point bravo". Entry "2 / 8".
key Right
wait 1
shot key-right

# PgDn (Next) goes forward. "Slide 3" and "Point charlie". Entry "3 / 8".
key Next
wait 1
shot key-pgdn

# Space goes forward. "Slide 4" and "Point delta". Entry "4 / 8".
key space
wait 1
shot key-space

# N goes forward. "Slide 5" and "Point echo". Entry "5 / 8".
key n
wait 1
shot key-n

# Left goes back. "Slide 4" and "Point delta". Entry "4 / 8".
key Left
wait 1
shot key-left

# PgUp (Prior) goes back. "Slide 3" and "Point charlie". Entry "3 / 8".
key Prior
wait 1
shot key-pgup

# Shift+Space goes back. "Slide 2" and "Point bravo". Entry "2 / 8".
key shift+space
wait 1
shot key-shift-space

# P goes back. "Slide 1" and "Point alpha". Entry "1 / 8".
key p
wait 1
shot key-p

# End goes to the last page. "Slide 8" and "Point hotel". Entry "8 / 8".
key End
wait 1
shot key-end

# Wheel down on the last slide does not flip past it. Still "Slide 8", entry "8 / 8".
click 602 472 5
wait 1
shot wheel-past-last

# Home goes to the first page. "Slide 1" and "Point alpha". Entry "1 / 8".
key Home
wait 1
shot key-home

# Down flips when the slide fits. "Slide 2", entry "2 / 8".
key Down
wait 1
shot key-down

# Up flips back. "Slide 1", entry "1 / 8".
key Up
wait 1
shot key-up

# The Previous button on the first slide does not flip before it. Still "Slide 1",
# entry "1 / 8".
click 540 48
wait 1
shot button-prev-first

# Wheel up on the first slide does not flip before it. Still "Slide 1", entry "1 / 8".
click 602 472 4
wait 1
shot wheel-past-first

# One wheel notch down flips one slide. "Slide 2", entry "2 / 8".
click 602 472 5
wait 1
shot wheel-notch-down

# Two notches 40 ms apart, the second inside 150 ms of the flip, flip one slide only.
# "Slide 3", entry "3 / 8". Not "Slide 4".
run xdotool click --repeat 2 --delay 40 5
wait 1
shot wheel-burst

# A notch more than 150 ms after the last flip flips again. "Slide 4", entry "4 / 8".
click 602 472 5
wait 1
shot wheel-after-lockout

# Wheel up flips back one slide. "Slide 3", entry "3 / 8".
click 602 472 4
wait 1
shot wheel-notch-up

# The Previous button goes back one slide. "Slide 2", entry "2 / 8".
click 540 48
wait 1
shot button-prev

# The Next button goes forward one slide. "Slide 3", entry "3 / 8".
click 610 48
wait 1
shot button-next

# Ctrl+Shift+L switches to Continuous and keeps page 3. Slide 3's top edge is at the top of
# the pane (y 69 or 81), its "Slide 3" heading and "Point charlie" line are at the top, and
# the top of slide 4 is below it at about y 492. Entry "3 / 8".
key ctrl+shift+l
wait 2
shot continuous-slide-3

# The Previous button in Continuous goes to page 2. "Slide 2" heading at the top of the
# pane, entry "2 / 8".
click 540 48
wait 2
shot continuous-prev-to-slide-2

# The Next button in Continuous goes to page 3. "Slide 3" heading at the top of the pane,
# entry "3 / 8". Identical in layout to continuous-slide-3.
click 610 48
wait 2
shot continuous-next-to-slide-3

# In Continuous, Right and Space do not flip (their old behaviour, nothing happens on a
# fitting width). The screen is identical to continuous-next-to-slide-3, entry "3 / 8".
click 602 150
key Right
wait 1
key space
wait 1
shot continuous-right-space

# Ctrl+Shift+L switches back to Single Page on slide 3. "Slide 3" is centered, entry
# "3 / 8", the same as button-next.
key ctrl+shift+l
wait 2
shot single-slide-3

# Click the chat input and type "N p n" (the spaces are Space presses too). The input
# shows "N p n". The PDF still shows "Slide 3", entry "3 / 8". No flip.
click 1180 800
type N p n
wait 1
shot chat-input-no-flip
